test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T22:57:26.1793537Z             "body": "This draft preserves original local stdio MCP and adds bounded batch/jobs, private profiles/artifacts, production packaging and lifecycle controls. Publishing remains disabled; release acceptance is blocked.\n\nCandidate732c913 adds a checkout-only journal timing preload and a separate macOS control after the normal actual-client matrix. Existing client/control jobs, action/RPC/test/job limits, production commands and browser/transport defaults remain unchanged. The fresh control reports completed RPCs from normally exiting instrumented processes; missing receipts do not confer exit/completeness authority. It is not a profile of a previous failing host. Actual local Node22/24 controls complete1000 in37.273/39.045s, modelTurns0/owned0, with timing-directory removal confirmed. A negative after two real tool discoveries and a real zero audit preserves primary+cleanup causes and both failed workspaces. The297-file production pack excludes the QA loader, evidence and portable reproducer;21 frozen source hashes still match the earlier successful Node22 production install/runtime-smoke check. Typecheck, README generation and actionlint pass;26-doc audit363 local targets/2 anchors has no issues.\n\nBrowser core remains reviewed9f9750ae24604e2099e1c1f6564d5d6cb3d19d30dfbc8b5ec61ba18c0989e25a: VP9 metadata, one exact capture-unavailable retry under the original deadline, and ordered existing viewport commands. No additional browser fix is claimed. A portable public-API reproducer yields7/8 short first JPEGs on Linux full Chromium156.0.8078.4. Passive frameResized/device-height metadata and real contents-size commands do not establish reliable capture readiness. No frame discard/seek, renderer warmup, encoder rewrite, input replay or rejected146 hidden-window change is shipped.\n\nLatest completed native97 at953ba87: batch39853792171 reports1631 passes/7 failures; original39853792190 reports599/6; completed summaries2230/13, reported skips/cancels0. Separately, macOS actual Codex fails TIMED_OUT969/failed970 interrupted, result available/opAttentionfalse, cleanup terminated/temp removed. Its failed acceptance workspace is not removed; final audit/appserver close observed. Linux/Windows actual1000 pass35.816/38.197s, model0/owned0. Earlier native96 Windows CRASHED75/journal progress timeout remains unresolved.\n\nAll five installed-package steps/both parent-death variants, all component lanes and12 actual schema races pass. All17 logs resolve; Linux22 first EOF after3545bytes is retained with successful ordinary retry. Batch Linux20/22/24 is209/0,212/1,212/1; Mac212/1 Windows201/4. Three stronger first-JPEG assertions fail despite completed ordering:320x180,320x153,131x98 (Mac metadata500x153). Assertions remain strict. The Mac group-hint control passes but does not recover native96's old nested failure facts. Windows SDK startup diagnostics are unselected because its client passes.\n\nWindows main Firefox fails11/23 actions, declarative9/23, a negative ambiguity timeout, and429 goto0/one hit. Positive locator19-action/six-effect checks finish before the negative failure; that negative's exact step/effect counters are not logged. Private/inherited/stock-headed controls each pass10fresh/230actions. Protocol-headed completes one run then3/23 (26total), pointer timeout; projected pending5 at failure/one mouse-dispatch after cleanup. Scoped before-force/final observations0 do not prove input completion. Four separate Mac transport controls pass1000 in106.346/116.486/117.994/109.530s; they do not waive the primary timeout.\n\nOriginal main Linux200/0 Mac198/2 Windows196/4 includes8 stock references each. PNG12/12 PCM10/12 video11/12. Windows WebKit stays ready0; Mac Chromium misses preload deadline then plays after activation. Both Firefox trusted-code tests exceed30s: Mac100-click assertions finish with browser_close pending; Windows unsafe tool remains pending, click count unknown. Original Mac video passes, all93 recorder-input headers320x240; no fresh Mac video controls run. This sample does not clear native96 gray/short input or current first-JPEG regressions. Windows legacy3/0, Docker2/0.\n\nFull process observations remain unfiltered by role/name/age/window. No hint-authorized signal, unsafe replay, lease/debt clearance or retrospective clearance of native94 survivor/native89 exits/historical136/142 gaps. Scope and full logs: docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md, docs/evidence/native97-summary.json and the portable capture reproduction. Native98 at732c913 is active: batch39859258163 and original39859258064. G18 BLOCKED; no merge/publication.",
